1
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:10,210
A photo shows a mountain reflected in a still lake.

2
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:12,940
The water line is perfectly horizontal.

3
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:16,010
The peak is 3 units above the water.

4
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:18,500
Where is the reflection of the peak?

5
00:00:18,550 --> 00:00:21,760
Pause the video and choose.

6
00:00:21,810 --> 00:00:26,860
A reflection is the same distance from the mirror line, on the other side.

7
00:00:26,910 --> 00:00:30,790
So the reflected peak is 3 units below the water.

8
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:33,670
Remember: x equals 3 is a vertical line.

9
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:37,170
y equals negative 1 is a horizontal line.

10
00:00:37,220 --> 00:00:44,020
Each image point is the same distance from the mirror line as the object point, but on the other side.

11
00:00:44,070 --> 00:00:46,980
Measure at right angles to the line.

12
00:00:47,030 --> 00:00:48,640
Reflect in x equals 2.

13
00:00:48,690 --> 00:00:52,040
The point 4, 2 is 2 to the right of the line.

14
00:00:52,090 --> 00:00:55,310
So its image is 2 to the left: 0, 2.

15
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:56,070
Your turn.

16
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:58,100
Reflect 5, 3 in x equals 2.

17
00:00:58,150 --> 00:01:01,540
Pause the video and try it.

18
00:01:01,590 --> 00:01:07,780
5, 3 is 3 to the right of the line, so its image is 3 to the left: negative 1, 3.

19
00:01:07,830 --> 00:01:12,090
Reflecting in the line y equals x swaps the coordinates.

20
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:14,020
3, 1 becomes 1, 3.

21
00:01:14,070 --> 00:01:19,570
To find a mirror line, find the midpoints between object points and their images.

22
00:01:19,620 --> 00:01:22,440
The mirror line goes through them.

23
00:01:22,490 --> 00:01:23,740
Here is the method.

24
00:01:23,790 --> 00:01:25,730
Step 1: draw the mirror line.

25
00:01:25,780 --> 00:01:31,560
x equals a is vertical, y equals b is horizontal, and y equals x is diagonal.

26
00:01:31,610 --> 00:01:37,170
Step 2: for each vertex, count the distance to the line, at right angles.

27
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:42,590
Step 3: count the same distance on the other side, and plot the image.

28
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:47,330
Step 4: check that the image is flipped, but the same size.

29
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:51,060
Reflect 1, 5 and 3, negative 1 in y equals 1.

30
00:01:51,110 --> 00:01:56,440
1, 5 is 4 above the line, so its image is 4 below: 1, negative 3.

31
00:01:56,490 --> 00:02:01,620
3, negative 1 is 2 below, so its image is 2 above: 3, 3.

32
00:02:01,670 --> 00:02:02,330
Your turn.

33
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:04,890
Reflect 4, 1 in the line y equals x.

34
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:07,860
Pause and work it out.

35
00:02:07,910 --> 00:02:09,710
Swap the coordinates.

36
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:11,850
4, 1 becomes 1, 4.

37
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:16,610
2, 5 maps to 2, negative 1, and 4, 6 maps to 4, negative 2.

38
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:19,190
The midpoints are 2, 2 and 4, 2.

39
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:22,170
They are both on the line y equals 2.

40
00:02:22,220 --> 00:02:24,660
That is the mirror line.

41
00:02:24,710 --> 00:02:27,770
Ivy reflects 5, 1 in the line x equals 3.

42
00:02:27,820 --> 00:02:29,830
Which line is wrong?

43
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:30,980
Line 1 is wrong.

44
00:02:31,030 --> 00:02:33,500
That is a reflection in the y axis.

45
00:02:33,550 --> 00:02:39,960
Count from x equals 3 instead: 5 is 2 to the right, so the image is 2 to the left.

46
00:02:40,010 --> 00:02:42,420
The image is 1, 1.

47
00:02:42,470 --> 00:02:47,340
The word ambulance is often painted back to front on the front of the vehicle.

48
00:02:47,390 --> 00:02:52,810
Drivers ahead see it in their rear-view mirror, reflected the right way round.

49
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:54,160
One last question.

50
00:02:54,210 --> 00:02:56,860
Reflect 0, 4 in the line y equals 1.

51
00:02:56,910 --> 00:03:00,290
Pause the video and answer.

52
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:03,250
0, 4 is 3 above the line y equals 1.

53
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:07,020
So its image is 3 below: 0, negative 2.

54
00:03:07,070 --> 00:03:13,240
To remember: same distance from the mirror line, on the other side, at right angles.

55
00:03:13,290 --> 00:03:14,820
x equals a is vertical.

56
00:03:14,870 --> 00:03:16,530
y equals b is horizontal.

57
00:03:16,580 --> 00:03:20,290
Reflecting in y equals x swaps the coordinates.

58
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:25,190
Find a mirror line from the midpoints of object and image pairs.

59
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:29,060
Reflections flip a shape, but keep it congruent.

60
00:03:29,110 --> 00:03:34,470
Great work! Now practise lesson 14.4 on Camday.
